  "body": "Found by the read-only second read of PR #3232 (comment 7077866674). The two items are not defects of the path. The option \"sharp corners\" leaves material on the part; it does not gouge.\n\n1. The note always says that the tightest inside corner keeps the radius of the wire. The worst leftover can also be a shallow notch that is narrower than two kerfs. That notch stays fully uncut. The note must name this case, or the planner must give a second note for it. No test has a narrow-notch profile with the option on: add one.\n2. With skim passes, only the note of the rough pass is kept. It gives a leftover that is larger than the final leftover. The note must give the leftover after the last skim pass.\n\nNot judged without a run, from the same read:\n- The position of the wire on the lower plane at a sharp corner, with the cone corner rule and a negative taper.\n- How the stock simulation shows the corner leftover.\n\nRefs #3207\n",
